xnu 0482: report the wifi stage without touching mmio

The ring is not a reliable transcript (it drops lines out of order, measured
2026-11-26), and `wifistat` reads `BAR0+0x28`, which wedges the AHB and the
command thread when the worker has not voted the rails -- that boot could not be
reset to fastboot.

A stage counter records how far the worker got (`2` thread entry, `4` pins
mapped, `6` supplies, `7` WLAN enabled, `8` GCC power, `9` host windows, `10`
PHY table, `12` link up, `13` identity, `15` SOC reset, `16` EXECENV read, `17`
doorbell, `18` status polled). `wifistage` returns it with the cached
`EXECENV`/`BHI_STATUS`/`ERRCODE` and never touches MMIO. `wifistat` also stops
reading the BAR below stage 9.
